      "dom_id": "question-60142",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "An animal shelter houses only dogs and cats. The ratio of dogs to cats is $4:3.$ If there are $32$ dogs, what is the total number of animals in the shelter?",
      "worked_solution": "We start with the ratio $4:3$ and write it as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{3}\n$$\n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the number of dogs and the denominator represents the number of cats.\n\nWe can make a numerator of $32$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $8:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{4\\times 8}{3\\times 8}=\\frac{32}{24}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there are $32$ dogs and $24$ cats. So the total number of animals in the animal shelter is\n\n$$\n32+24=56.\n$$",
